<title>UK: Queens Moat says sale to Cliveden approved.</title>
<headline>Queens Moat says sale to Cliveden approved.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British hotel group Queens Moat Houses Plc said on Monday that the sale of its Royal Crecent Hotel in Bath to Cliveden Plc was now unconditional following approval by Cliveden shareholders and by Queens Moat's debenture holders.</p>
<p>Completion of the deal, worth 8.5 million stg, is due to take place on Tuesday, the company added in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
